      "text": "I am deciding how to name the folders of a new project. Do you prefer short names or descriptive ones?",
      "id": 1
    },
    {
      "at": 1792000004000,
      "kind": "assistant",
      "text": "Descriptive, as long as they stay short enough to read in one glance. A name like \"billing\" tells you what is inside and costs nothing to type, while \"b\" or \"module-2\" sends you to open the folder to find out.\n\nThe test I use: if someone new reads the list of folders with no explanation, can they guess where to look for a given piece of work? If yes, the names are good enough. If you find yourself writing a README just to explain the names, they are too short.",
